      `the depreciation taken for periods after May 6, 1997` IS A NUMBER @desc How much depreciation was taken, or was allowable, on the home for periods after May 6, 1997, in dollars? Enter 0 if none. (Section 1250(b)(3) says what counts; it is not among our sources.)
      `I elect not to have section 121 apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect not to have section 121 apply to this sale? (Answer no unless you have chosen to leave the whole gain in your gross income.)
      `my spouse died before the sale and I have not remarried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your spouse dead on the date of the sale, and are you unmarried now? Answer no if your spouse is alive or if you have remarried.
      `the date my spouse died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse die? If your spouse is not dead, enter any date.
      `my late spouse owned the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your spouse is dead: did your late spouse own the home? Answer no if your spouse is not dead.
      `the date my late spouse became an owner` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your late spouse become an owner? Your late spouse is taken to have owned it from then until death. If none, enter any date.
      `my late spouse lived in it as their main home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your late spouse live in the home as their main home? Answer no if your spouse is not dead.
      `the date my late spouse's stay began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your late spouse's stay in the home as their main home begin? If none, enter any date.
      `the date my late spouse's stay ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your late spouse's stay in the home as their main home end? If none, enter any date.
      `my late spouse sold another home earlier and left its gain out of gross income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before this sale, did your late spouse sell or exchange another home and leave its gain out of gross income under this section? Answer no if your spouse is not dead.
      `the date of my late spouse's most recent earlier sale` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your late spouse's most recent earlier sale of that kind? If none, enter any date.
      `I have become physically or mentally incapable of self-care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become physically or mentally incapable of self-care?
      `the date I moved into the facility` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you move into the facility? If you were in none, enter any date.
      `the date I left the facility` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you leave it? If you were still there when you sold, enter the date of the sale. If you were in none, enter any date.
      `the facility is licensed to care for someone in my condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the facility licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in your condition? (A nursing home counts.) Answer no if you were in none.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my gain is left out filing alone` IS
    `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` facts
    WHERE
        me MEANS `the taxpayer who may be a surviving spouse or in a care facility` `the date I sold the home` `the date I became an owner` `the date my first stay began` `the date my first stay ended` `I lived in it as my main home a second time` `the date my second stay began` `the date my second stay ended` `I sold another home earlier and left its gain out of my gross income` `the date of my most recent earlier sale` `I have become physically or mentally incapable of self-care` `the date I moved into the facility` `the date I left the facility` `the facility is licensed to care for someone in my condition` `my spouse died before the sale and I have not remarried` `the date my spouse died` `my late spouse owned the home` `the date my late spouse became an owner` `my late spouse lived in it as their main home` `the date my late spouse's stay began` `the date my late spouse's stay ended` `my late spouse sold another home earlier and left its gain out of gross income` `the date of my late spouse's most recent earlier sale`
