        spouse MEANS `the spouse who may have owned or lived in the home` `the date I sold the home` `my spouse owned the home` `the date my spouse became an owner` `my spouse lived in it as their main home` `the date my spouse's stay began` `the date my spouse's stay ended` `my spouse sold another home earlier and left its gain out of gross income` `the date of my spouse's most recent earlier sale`
        facts MEANS `the facts of a sale of a home, with the election under (f)` `the date I sold the home` `my gain on the sale` TRUE me spouse (`the depreciation a taxpayer states` `the date I sold the home` `the depreciation taken for periods after May 6, 1997`) `I sold because my place of employment changed` `I sold by reason of health` `I sold by reason of unforeseen circumstances that the regulations count` `I elect not to have section 121 apply`

§ `Things that take my sale out of the section (subsections (d)(5), (d)(8), (d)(10), (e), (f))`

@export Does section 121 reach my sale at all (s 121(d)(5)(A), (d)(8), (d)(10), (e), (f))?
GIVEN `the date I sold the home` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you sell (or exchange) your home?
      `what happened to my home` IS AN `Event in respect of the property` @desc What happened to your home?
      `I elect not to have section 121 apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect not to have section 121 apply to this sale?
      `section 877(a)(1) treatment applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1) apply to you? (Section 877 is not among our sources.)
      `I got the home in a like-kind exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get the home in an exchange in which gain was not recognized under section 1031(a) or (b)? (Section 1031 is not among our sources.)
      `the seller in that exchange was me or someone whose basis follows mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person who made the exchange, or someone whose basis in the home is worked out from the basis of the person who did? Answer no if you got no home in a like-kind exchange.
      `the date I got the home in the exchange` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you get the home in that exchange? If you did not, enter any date.
      `the interest I sold is a remainder interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest you sold a remainder interest in the home?
      `I elect that section 121 not fail to apply to a remainder interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a remainder interest, do you elect that section 121 not fail to apply because of that?
      `another interest in the home was sold separately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was another interest in the home sold or exchanged separately from the one you sold?
      `I sold to a related person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sell to, or exchange with, a person related to you as described in section 267(b) or 707(b)? (Those sections are not among our sources.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 121 reach my sale at all` IS
    CONSIDER `s 121 whether the section reaches the sale or exchange` facts
    WHEN `Section 121 applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): layer 1's "does not apply" is the text's own flat negative: "This section shall not apply ..." ((d)(8)(A), (d)(10), (e), (f)).
    WHEN `Section 121 does not apply because` why THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (as layer 1 gives it: silent, or limited by its own wording): the event is not listed, or a remainder interest has no election or was sold to a related person.
    WHEN `Not covered because` why THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        me MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) FALSE (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) (Date 1 1 1900) EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY `section 877(a)(1) treatment applies to me`
        facts MEANS `the facts of a sale` `the date I sold the home` `what happened to my home` 0 FALSE me `no spouse` EMPTY `I elect not to have section 121 apply` `I got the home in a like-kind exchange` `the seller in that exchange was me or someone whose basis follows mine` `the date I got the home in the exchange` `the interest I sold is a remainder interest` `I elect that section 121 not fail to apply to a remainder interest` `another interest in the home was sold separately` `I sold to a related person` EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- (d)(5)(A)
@export Is what happened to my home treated as a sale of it (s 121(d)(5)(A))?
GIVEN `what happened to my home` IS AN `Event in respect of the property` @desc What happened to your home?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what happened to my home treated as a sale` IS
    `s 121(d)(5)(A) the event counts as a sale or exchange for this section` `what happened to my home`

-- (d)(5)(B)
@export For a home that was destroyed, stolen, seized or condemned, what is the amount realized when section 1033 is applied (s 121(d)(5)(B))?
GIVEN `the amount realized, determined without regard to section 121` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the amount realized, in dollars, determined without regard to section 121?
      `the gain not included in my gross income by reason of section 121` IS A NUMBER @desc How much gain, in dollars, is not included in your gross income pursuant to section 121?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the amount realized for section 1033` IS
    `s 121(d)(5)(B) the amount realized in applying section 1033` `the amount realized, determined without regard to section 121` `the gain not included in my gross income by reason of section 121`

§ `Counting time as owned or lived in: care, divorce and earlier homes (subsections (d)(3), (d)(7), (g))`

-- (d)(7): only if the taxpayer has become physically or mentally incapable of self-care.
@export For how many days does my stay in a care facility count as living in my home (s 121(d)(7))?
GIVEN `the date I sold the home` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you sell (or exchange) your home?
      `the date I became an owner` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become an owner of the home? You are taken to have owned it from then until the sale.
      `the date my first stay began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you first start to live in the home as your main home?
      `the date my first stay ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your first stay in the home as your main home end? If you were still living there when you sold, enter the date of the sale.
      `I have become physically or mentally incapable of self-care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become physically or mentally incapable of self-care?
      `the date I moved into the facility` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you move into the facility?
      `the date I left the facility` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you leave it? If you were still there when you sold, enter the date of the sale.
      `the facility is licensed to care for someone in my condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the facility licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in your condition? (A nursing home counts.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many days does my stay in a care facility count` IS
    CONSIDER `s 121(d)(7) the taxpayer is treated as using the property as the principal residence while residing in a licensed facility` `I have become physically or mentally incapable of self-care` (Holding OF (LIST Span OF `the date I became an owner`, `the date I sold the home`), (LIST Span OF `the date my first stay began`, `the date my first stay ended`)) (`s 121(a) the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange` `the date I sold the home`) `the date I sold the home` stays
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a taxpayer who (A) becomes physically or mentally incapable of self-care, and (B) owns property and uses such property ... for periods aggregating at least 1 year"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deemed THEN JUST (`the days in the spans of a list` deemed)
    WHERE
        stays MEANS LIST `Stay in a facility` WITH
            `days` IS (Span OF `the date I moved into the facility`, `the date I left the facility`)
            `facility licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in the taxpayer's condition` IS `the facility is licensed to care for someone in my condition`

-- (g): section 1034 is repealed; the question is for a home bought under it.
@export How many days of my earlier homes count toward the 2 years, where I bought this home under section 1034 (s 121(g))?
GIVEN `I bought this home in a rollover that left part of the gain on my earlier home unrecognized under section 1034` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you buy this home in a rollover under section 1034, as it stood on the day before section 121 was enacted, that left part of the gain on your earlier home unrecognized? (Section 1034 is repealed and is not among our sources.)
      `the days my earlier home and each home before it were owned and used as my main home` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in all were your earlier home, and each home before it, owned and used by you as your main home?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of my earlier homes count` IS
    `s 121(g) the days the other residence was owned and used are included` `I bought this home in a rollover that left part of the gain on my earlier home unrecognized under section 1034` `the days my earlier home and each home before it were owned and used as my main home`

-- (d)(3)(B), (d)(3)(C): a former spouse is granted use of the home under a divorce or separation instrument.
-- The answer is a number of days, so the question asks for days: where the text does not speak (no divorce or separation instrument), the answer is NOTHING, not 0 and not a "no".
@export For how many days while my spouse or former spouse is granted the use of the home under our divorce or separation do I count as living in it (s 121(d)(3))?
GIVEN `the date I sold the home` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you sell (or exchange) your home?
      `the date I became an owner` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become an owner of the home? You are taken to have owned it from then until the sale.
      `the date my spouse or former spouse was granted use` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your spouse or former spouse granted use of the home?
      `the date that use ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that use end? If it was still going when you sold, enter the date of the sale.
      `a decree of divorce or separate maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the use granted under a decree of divorce or separate maintenance?
      `a written instrument incident to such a decree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it granted under a written instrument incident to such a decree?
      `a written separation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it granted under a written separation agreement?
      `a decree requiring support payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it granted under a decree that requires one spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many days do I count as living in my home while my former spouse has the use` IS
    CONSIDER `s 121(d)(3)(B) the individual is treated as using the property as the principal residence while a spouse or former spouse is granted use` (LIST Span OF `the date I became an owner`, `the date I sold the home`) (LIST grant)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during any period of ownership while such individual's spouse or former spouse is granted use of the property under a divorce or separation instrument"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deemed THEN JUST (`the days in the spans of a list` deemed)
    WHERE
        grant MEANS `Use granted` WITH
            `days` IS (Span OF `the date my spouse or former spouse was granted use`, `the date that use ended`)
            `instrument` IS (Instrument WITH
                `a decree of divorce or separate maintenance` IS `a decree of divorce or separate maintenance`
                `a written instrument incident to such a decree` IS `a written instrument incident to such a decree`
                `a written separation agreement` IS `a written separation agreement`
                `a decree requiring a spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other spouse` IS `a decree requiring support payments`)
